I am a final-year Bachelor of Information Management student with a strong interest in software quality assurance and technology. I would describe myself as a curious, adaptable, and growth-oriented individual who enjoys understanding how things work and finding ways to make them better. Over time, I have developed a particular interest in software testing, where I get to combine analytical thinking, problem-solving, and technical skills.

My experience in software quality assurance has taught me to look beyond whether a feature simply works. I enjoy understanding business requirements, exploring different scenarios, identifying edge cases, and thinking about how a small defect can impact an entire system. Having worked with financial software, I have also learned the importance of understanding business logic and how different modules interact with one another. Alongside manual and API testing, I have been developing my automation skills using Playwright and TypeScript, while continuously strengthening my understanding of software development and testing practices.

Beyond my technical interests, I genuinely value learning through collaboration and taking initiative. I have participated in mentorship programs, contributed to collaborative projects, and been involved in organizing software testing workshops as a college ambassador. These experiences have helped me improve my communication, teamwork, and ability to learn from people with different perspectives. I also appreciate constructive feedback because I see it as an opportunity to identify my weaknesses and become better.

If there is one thing that defines me, it is my willingness to learn and step outside my comfort zone. I don't consider myself someone who knows everything, but I am someone who is willing to put in the effort to figure things out. I enjoy challenges that push me to think differently, take responsibility, and grow. At this stage of my career, my goal is to become a well-rounded QA professional who not only understands the technical side of software quality but also understands the value of building reliable products that genuinely solve problems.